       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg. Please confirm what you intended. Typical dosing for adults is:\n\n- **Depression, OCD, or anxiety:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **PTSD or panic disorder:** start at 25 mg once daily, then increase to 50 mg after one week and titrate from there. The maximum is 200 mg/day.\n\nOnce you give me the corrected dose, I'll enter the order right away. If 1000 mg is truly what you want, for example in an overdose or other unusual situation, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest a pharmacist or the attending review it first."
